**Lemma 4.1 (matching-write table for both reservoirs).** On
$\mathcal C_{\mathrm{gc}}$, let $j$ be the absolute ordinal immediately
before a variable IN. Its matching retained write has post-row ordinal
$w$ and the following actual location and latch.

| Actual reader | Retained wire location fixed before IN | $w$ | Pending latch |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 70 outer first/second gate bit | Its old append R, made a cell by EX | $j+3$ | 6 |
| 70 separate HistoryMode | Its own old append R | $j+3$ | 6 |
| 70 history tag, length or tested payload bit | Its old append R | $j+3$ | 6 |
| 13 source header or length bit | Its old append R | $j+3$ | 5 |
| 13 source preallocated payload bit | Its already positioned payload cell | $j+2$ | 5 |
